What an agent needs to finish a card checkout on the Camofox tab.

Symptoms (a hosted card form, Stripe-style): browser_vision showed the
vault-filled card fields in plain text; the captcha sat in a nested
cross-origin frame no ref reached and there was no way to click a point;
16 k-char snapshots of the same page were re-read five times.

- browser_vision: a 409 from the server (camofox-browser's vault mask cannot
  mask a filled field, ../camofox-browser/vault-frames-plugin/mask.js) is
  reported as capture_refused with what to do instead, never retried around;
  the result carries the viewport (X-Camofox-Viewport) and how to click a
  point of it.
- browser_click: x and y instead of a ref click that point of the viewport
  (POST /tabs/<id>/click-at, ../camofox-browser/captcha-plugin), whatever
  frame is there. A ref already reaches controls inside iframes.
- browser_snapshot: `scope` keeps the subtrees whose line contains the text
  (a frame, a form), `diff` only the lines changed since this task's last
  snapshot of the same page and scope. Both are cut from the same redacted,
  masked snapshot.
Not upstream (hermes-official-plugins).

